","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $511K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 37%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $92K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $48K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Remitly Global, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $4.8B market cap on $1.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +36% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +3.3pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -44% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $296M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 18 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.79\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 10.2\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.5%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 5.3% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.047048171056874304},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $12.0M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Growing faster than most Technology peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(RELY) Risk Channels and Responsive Allocation","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/52/RELY_Risk_Channels_and_Responsive_Allocation_111326065201_1794570721.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794570721.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.202,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Remitly Global (NASDAQ:RELY) Share Price Breaks Above 50 Day Moving Average Following Insider Selling","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/re